1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,000
Confidant: a compliant shielded pool on the XRP Ledger.
Live on confidant.im, XRPL testnet.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
On a public ledger every payment is a disclosure.
Confidant hides the graph: who paid whom, and how much.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Shield into the pool, transfer privately inside it, unshield to any address.
On the ledger you see only an anchor, never a link.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Built at the hackathon: lending on shielded capital.
A credential gate, and a proof of funds a lender reads from the ledger.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:28,000
The Mastercard track: an agent with shielded funds
pays RLUSD through AP4M for the relay of a private transfer.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Balances: what the notes are worth,
and what the pool account holds on the ledger.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Every drop of the difference is accounted for,
live from the ledger.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The app. Left: the public XRPL account, with its entry credential.
Right: the private pool wallet. Keys never leave the browser.

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Shield: move 10 XRP from the account into the pool.

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Prove: the zero-knowledge proof is built here, in the browser.

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Deposit: a public Payment to the pool, with a memo.

12
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Anchor: the verifiers wait until the deposit is 2 ledgers old,
then 2 of 3 signers re-check the proof and anchor it.

13
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Done: a private note of 9.975 XRP (10 less the 0.25% fee).
Proved in 5.5 s on 8 threads.

14
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:01,000
On the explorer: the deposit, a public Payment to the pool account.

15
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:08,000
And the anchor: the pool account's transaction
that records the new state in its memo.

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Transfer: pay any address inside the pool.
Nothing reaches the ledger but the anchor.

17
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Unshield: a note becomes a payout to any XRPL address,
here back to the user's own account.

18
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Prove funds: one button.
"Prove I hold 59.85 XRP", the whole private balance.

19
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The previous proof-of-funds credential is removed first,
then the browser proves afresh.

20
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Record: every signer re-checks the proof on its own node;
the quorum writes the credential on the XRPL account.

21
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Confirm: the account accepts it with its own signature.

22
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Refresh: fresh notes, so this proof cannot be linked
to the next payment.

23
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:20,000
The lender's page: one address, Check.
"Controlled at least 59.85 XRP as of that ledger", signed by 2 of 3.

24
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:28,000
On the explorer: the ConfidantPoF credential (XLS-70).
Issuer: the pool. Expires in 24 hours.

25
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:36,000
CredentialAccept: signed by the holder's own account.

26
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:43,000
The refresh's anchor: the pool account's transaction
with the new state in its memo.

27
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Notes refreshed: 59.85 XRP now sits in fresh notes.
The receipt can be downloaded; nothing secret in it.

28
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Audit: hand an auditor the viewing key.
Full history of this wallet, nothing about others, read-only.

29
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:15,000
From here the screen is blank: the walkthrough moved to a private window,
which this window recording did not capture.

30
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Off screen: a fresh browser, as a first-time visitor.
Create wallet: the spending key is generated in the browser.

31
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:42,000
The new XRPL testnet account is funded from the faucet,
about 10 to 30 seconds, nothing to press.

32
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:56,000
First shield: the app asks the demo issuer for the entry credential (ConfidantKYC),
and the account confirms it with its own signature.

33
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:04,000
KYC in demo mode: the gate is the real system;
the demo issuer's admission policy is open registration.

34
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:09,800
Then the shield runs as above.
Try it yourself: confidant.im, in a private window.
